-that gate. `audit --regenerate` must cover every accumulated document before a
-gate and after the last parser change. The parser fingerprint records code
-changes within the existing schema/parser release contract.
-
-`select-local --wave N` verifies source hashes/completeness and selects unused
-local RAW using the configured quotas and diversity hints. It performs no
-network requests. Repeated `--exclude-document-id` arguments protect additional
-previously reviewed identities. `inventory-local` writes the canonical identity,
-URL, completeness, duplicate and role evidence to
-`evidence/local_raw_inventory.json`; unusable captures never count.
-
-`--progress-dir` maintains atomic overall progress in `evidence/state.json` and
-human recovery instructions in `checkpoint.md` and `resume.md`. State is saved
-after each capture, selection, extraction and document audit, and after each
-completed cumulative validation. Repair/test/source-review evidence must also
-be persisted before proceeding. On interruption, reconcile these files with
-actual RAW/Extract manifests and git status, then continue the first unfinished
-step. Never recrawl complete RAW or trust a stale parser fingerprint.
-
-Use a separate `--extracted-dir` for current accumulated validations to preserve
-the reproducibility of historical reports and their recorded output hashes.
-Historical parser artifacts are evidence, not current acceptance outputs.
-Reports distinguish actual new network captures from reused local documents.
-
