-### Total-corpus reports and partial waves
-
-`inventory-local` accepts repeated `--baseline-manifest` and `--capture-fixture`
-arguments to record sample and reviewed-capture membership without counting a
-source identity twice. Keep the canonical inventory and target manifest under
-the total milestone's evidence directory. Target assembly can remain incomplete;
-do not fill it with duplicate identities or incomplete captures.
-
-`--wave-offset` gives later configured subruns continuous progress numbering.
-A partial local subrun is not automatically a completed hardening wave: when
-`--progress-dir` records an incomplete overall target, `complete-wave` rejects
-a partial final subrun wave. Keep those already processed documents pending and
-add only the documents needed to finish their 20-document wave. A shorter final
-wave is permitted when the overall target has actually been assembled.
-
-The generic report action also accepts `--target-manifest`. It reads cumulative
-audits from `--sample-manifest`, source reviews from
-`evidence/cumulative_reviews.json`, and optional narrative/completion evidence
